@startuml multiple-cursors-component
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

title Multiple Cursors (roadmap A3) — what each role adds

package "crates/ui (role 2)" {
  package "editor" {
    [input.rs\nIntent + 5 variants,\nintent_for, apply_intent] as IN
    [double_tap.rs\nDoubleTap\npress / is_armed / disarm] as DT
    [geometry.rs\ncolumn_of,\ncolumn_selections] as GEO
    [mod.rs\nhandle_mouse: ⌥Click,\ncolumn-mode drag] as W
    [EditorState\n+ alt_tap, column_mode,\ncolumn_anchor] as ST
  }
  [render.rs\ntab strip: COLUMN chip] as APP
}

package "crates/core (role 1)" {
  [text/find.rs\nnext_occurrence,\nall_occurrences\n(capped at MAX_OCCURRENCES)] as FIND
  [Selections\n+ push_primary, remove_primary,\n+ remove_at, index_at] as SEL
  [Selections::new\nsort + merge + re-point primary] as NORM
  [TextBuffer\ntype_text / apply\n(one Transaction)] as TB
}

IN --> FIND : needle -> ranges
IN --> SEL : add / remove / collapse
IN --> TB : edits, unchanged from A2
W --> ST
W --> DT : ⌥ edge + frame time
W --> GEO : drag rectangle ->\none Selection per line
W --> SEL : ⌥Click -> push_primary
DT --> IN : armed? ↑/↓ becomes CloneCaret
GEO --> SEL
SEL --> NORM
APP --> ST : column_mode()

note bottom of NORM
  Every operation is expressed through
  Selections::new — so "sorted, merged,
  non-empty, primary re-pointed" holds
  without any new normalisation (§4.1-4.2).
end note

note right of TB
  A3 adds no edit path: N cursors already
  produce one Transaction and one undo
  step since A1/A2 (§3.7).
end note

note right of FIND
  MAX_OCCURRENCES = 1000, same value and
  reason as search::MAX_SEARCH_RESULTS:
  a one-character needle in a large file
  would otherwise make ⌃⌘G a UI hang (§4.8).
end note

note left of DT
  The minimal double-tap detector
  roadmap §5.1 assigns to A3;
  G2 generalises it into the
  command registry.
end note

@enduml
